{"step_index":1706,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:57:39Z","input_tokens":2928,"cache_read_tokens":191573,"output_tokens":2011,"content":"The GST tax extraction, intra-state vs inter-state auto-determination, and quick preset click handler have been fixed and verified.\n\n---\n\n### Key Updates Applied\n\n#### 1. Strict Tax Extraction Without Wattage/Quantity Leakage ([`utils/invoiceTextParser.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js#L450-L490))\n- **Summary Zone Restriction:** GST extraction is strictly confined to the document's `summaryZone` and no longer scans generic two-digit numbers. Item wattage (e.g., `'20W'`) and quantities (e.g., `'Pack of 20'`) are completely ignored.\n- **Strict RegEx Patterns:**\n  - **CGST:** `/(?:CGST|Central GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i`\n  - **SGST:** `/(?:SGST|State GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i`\n  - **IGST:** `/(?:IGST|Integrated GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i`\n\n#### 2. Intra-State vs Inter-State Auto-Determination ([`utils/invoiceTextParser.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js#L500-L545), [`utils/auditEngine.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/auditEngine.js#L205-L250))\n- **State Code Matching:** Compares the first 2 digits of the Supplier GSTIN (e.g., `06`) and Buyer GSTIN (e.g., `06`):\n  - **Matching State Codes (Intra-State, e.g. `06 == 06`):**\n    - `igst` is set strictly to `0.00`.\n    - Default tax split uses CGST + SGST (9% + 9% = 18%, producing ₹990.00 CGST and ₹990.00 SGST on a ₹11,000 subtotal).\n    - Audit engine warns if IGST is erroneously billed on an intra-state invoice.\n  - **Differing State Codes (Inter-State, e.g. `07 != 06`):**\n    - `cgst = 0.00`, `sgst = 0.00`.\n    - `igst` is set to 18% (₹1,980.00 on ₹11,000).\n    - Audit engine warns if CGST or SGST is billed on an inter-state invoice.\n\n#### 3. Click Handler Sync for `[18% (Electrical)]` ([`components/AuditScorecard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/AuditScorecard.js#L765-L810))\n- Clicking `[18% (Electrical)]` (or any `data-gst-preset` button):\n  - Recalculates dynamically against the current Subtotal:\n    $$\\text{taxAmount} = \\text{round2}(\\text{subtotal} \\times 0.18)$$\n  - Evaluates Supplier vs. Buyer state codes:\n    - Intra-State: Sets `cgst = ₹990.00`, `sgst = ₹990.00`, `igst = 0.00`.\n    - Inter-State: Sets `cgst = 0.00`, `sgst = 0.00`, `igst = ₹1,980.00`.\n  - Directly updates the input DOM elements and calls `onUpdateHeader(\"gst_preset\", ...)`.\n  - Instantly triggers `recomputeEverything()`, re-running the full audit and updating the UI in real time.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Regex & Wattage Exclusion:** Verified that `'LED Tube Light 20W'` and `'Pack of 20'` do not match GST tax extractors.\n- **Intra-State Split:** Verified that with Subtotal ₹11,000 and matching `06` state codes, CGST = ₹990.00, SGST = ₹990.00, and IGST = 0.\n- **Inter-State Split:** Verified that with Subtotal ₹11,000 and differing state codes (`07` vs `06`), CGST = 0, SGST = 0, and IGST = ₹1,980.00.\n- **Server Reloaded:** The FastAPI backend daemon has been restarted and is live at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).","thinking":"The server is running; the focus shifts to the modified files. The invoice parsing utility now includes a helper function for tax extraction from specific line matches. The tax extraction logic enforces precise pattern matching within the summary zone for CGST and SGST.\n\n\nRevised the tax extraction to use more robust regex patterns for CGST, SGST, and IGST to avoid misidentifying other numerical values. Implemented logic to automatically determine intra-state or inter-state transactions based on GSTIN prefixes, setting IGST to zero for intra-state transactions. Added audit verification for GST calculations, ensuring consistency based on transaction type. Updated the user interface to dynamically calculate and apply tax based on subtotal and transaction type with instant feedback and re-auditing.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":1707,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:00:38Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nCRITICAL FIX: GST Tax extraction is injecting 2990 into CGST/SGST instead of 990.\n\n1. FIX THE DEFAULT TAX AUTO-CALCULATION:\n   - When GST is 18% Intra-State on a subtotal of ₹11,000.00:\n     * CGST @ 9% = 990.00 (NOT 2990.00)\n     * SGST @ 9% = 990.00 (NOT 2990.00)\n     * IGST = 0.00\n     * Total Tax = 1,980.00\n   - NEVER hallucinate the tax by taking (Billed Total - Subtotal). Calculate tax strictly as:\n     tax = subtotal * (rate_percentage / 100).\n\n2. FIX REGEX EXTRACTION OF PRINTED TAX VALUES:\n   - Match the exact printed tax lines on the bill:\n     Search for \"CGST @ 9%\" -> extract 990.00\n     Search for \"SGST @ 9%\" -> extract 990.00\n   - Ensure the regex does not prepend a stray '2' (e.g. from state code '06' or line 2) to the number '990.00'.\n\n3. MAKE QUICK GST BUTTONS AUTOCALCULATE:\n   - Clicking '[18% (Electrical)]' should immediately set:\n     cgst = subtotal * 0.09;\n     sgst = subtotal * 0.09;\n     igst = 0;\n   - Trigger the math recalculation immediately so Verified Total becomes 12,980.00.\n\nKEEP ALL EXISTING UI LAYOUT, SEC 44AD ITR-4 INSIGHTS, AND TABLE CONTROLS UNTOUCHED. \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-03T01:30:38+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
